{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact plan 035 stop head 83998083d93db3d038e6db42b31069e5e214d8da on builder/typed-core-stop-20261104, tree 71d6744a, for request 38662c56 under promise 54361847 and review request 9fc489c5. This approval covers the ten note paths at this head and the decision to stop. It does not review or approve the experiment source at 27d0e268, and it schedules none of M3 to M8.\n\nScope. Main 61497e21 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The four commits from 61497e21 add only files under notes/, and the commit-message check passes for all four. No source, test, dependency or card path changes. Gate commit 105bcb9c has tree 23fa5e10. Only the stop note and the gate manifest change after it.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The stop is correct, and the arithmetic holds. At 61497e21, the seven modules count 647, 268, 165, 532, 360, 266 and 616 lines, 2,854 in all, so one fifth is 571. The gross credit is 1,346: all 1,325 lines of guards, lists, effects and sends, plus the 21-line operand dispatcher. The 17 restored leaf ranges in deletion.json each span the lines they claim and sum to 327. The six replacement files at 27d0e268 hash to their recorded digests and count 95, 157, 16, 89, 178 and 30 lines, 565 in all. 1,346 − 327 − 565 = 454, which is 15.9% of 2,854 and 117 lines short. The estimate charges nothing for the remaining vocabulary and credits whole modules, so a real migration would fall further short.\n- The other two conditions hold. consumer.txt shows the CLI line with `acts.water.guards.1`, the deadline and the clock, read from one captured evaluation. The first full comparison passed the same day, well before the 11 November deadline. The note limits the consumer claim to a scratch CLI over scripted state.\n- The baseline holds. All 22 hashes in baseline.json match the files at 61497e21.\n- The experiment stays out of main. origin holds builder/typed-core-prototype-20261104 at 27d0e268, and this head adds none of its files.\n- The final affected union passes 40 cases in six files. Each of the two controls changes one source fragment and passes its selected case before the fault, with 14 others filtered out. Each then fails that case by assertion and restores exact source. The record keeps both compiler failures and the failed trace assertion.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0. All five stages pass: kernel, node, counting, plain and native. The counts are 135 node, 56 counting, 3,912 plain with one skip and 1,090 native with two skips. before.json and after.json record head 105bcb9c, tree 23fa5e10, a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43. receipt.json shows exit 0, unchanged source and no owned process left after 1,604.8 seconds.\n\nEvidence. The two manifests list 26 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and the scan finds no credential. All 41 selected gate originals match, the gate's private inventory of 2,278 files matches with no unlisted file, and every file has mode 0400. The 11 prototype units hold 874 files, all matching their SHA256SUMS, with retention set to at least 4 December 2026.\n\nArchitecture: sound decision. The plan packet stays on record as design, and the measured estimate shows the retained-leaf design would not pay for its migration. The packet already requires a new sketch and Hugh's approval before any later attempt.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Nothing here runs, deploys or changes authority.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One gap: the stop note links both manifests but does not state their SHA-256 digests, which the other evidence notes do. Record them in the next note that cites this evidence.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:148ba8c5d5f0821c894046aba04be8577628c78c","binding":"assigned","head":"83998083d93db3d038e6db42b31069e5e214d8da","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:db9dc1b7e69ec7365fe37fd409839c594f00